› Setup Q4

  The settings you just changed feed every configuration file
  abcd derives for this repository. A derived file that is
  not rebuilt keeps the old settings until the next install.

  Should abcd rebuild the derived files now?

› 1. Rebuild every derived configuration file
     Every file abcd derives is written again from the new
     settings. Files you edited by hand are left alone.
  2. Keep the files unchanged
     Nothing is written now. The files catch up at the next install.
  3. Decide later
     Nothing changes now. abcd asks again when the settings next change.

  Now: the files hold the old settings
  Change later: not applicable
